    "user_request_original": "Design a 17-layer defect cavity stack on silicon substrate with air incidence. Structure: Air | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | SiO2_defect | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | HfO2 | SiO2 | Si. Optimize all 17 layer thicknesses (bounds 200-3000 nm) to maximize emissivity in 8000-13000 nm band while minimizing emissivity in 3000-5000 nm band. Use normal incidence, unpolarized light. Materials: HfO2 (high index), SiO2 (low index and defect layer). Total layer count exactly 17 finite layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
